## **Description**

We are seeking clarification regarding the exact payload structure expected in W3C Verifiable credentials ([Appendix B.1.3.2](https://openid.net/specs/openid-4-verifiable-presentations-1_0.html#name-ldp-vcs)) when cryptographic holder binding is not requested by the Verifier.

The specification currently states:

> If require_cryptographic_holder_binding is set to true in the Credential Query, the Wallet MUST return a Verifiable Presentation of a Verifiable Credential. Otherwise, a Verifiable Credential without Holder Binding MUST be returned.

## Context & Request for Clarification

When `require_cryptographic_holder_binding` is evaluated as false, the phrase "a Verifiable Credential without Holder Binding MUST be returned" can be interpreted in two distinct ways by implementers. To ensure seamless interoperability between different Wallet and Verifier implementations, we would appreciate explicit guidance on which of the following structures is intended:

1. _A raw Verifiable Credential_: The Wallet returns only the bare VC payload (e.g., JSON LD LDP VC as issued by issuer), bypassing the Verifiable Presentation (VP) envelope entirely.

```
{
  "@context": [
    "https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1",
    "https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/examples/v1",
    "https://w3id.org/security/suites/ed25519-2020/v1"
  ],
  "id": "http://example.edu/credentials/3732",
  "type": [
    "VerifiableCredential",
    "UniversityDegreeCredential"
  ],
  "issuer": "https://example.edu/issuers/565049",
  "issuanceDate": "2010-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "credentialSubject": {
    // ... data
  },
  "proof": {
    //... proof contents
  }
}
```

2. _A Verifiable Presentation envelope without proof_: The Wallet returns a standard VP envelope wrapping the internal VC, but omits the outer proof object or signature.

```
{
  "@context": [
    "https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1",
    "https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/examples/v1"
  ],
  "id": "urn:uuid:39...a3903c5",
  "type": ["VerifiablePresentation"],
  "verifiableCredential": [{ /*Credential(s) to be shared*/ }],
}
```


Could you please help clarify the exact schema and wrapping behavior required here?

