This was originally to support the Relay State parameter, but we think it is a good idea to make this extensible to support any additional parameters defined in SAML as well as custom parameters.

This proposal adds a new “parameters” object to the `urn:ietf:params:fastfed:1.0:authentication:saml:2.0:enterprise` object in application metadata defined in section 3.1.2.

`parameters` object shape \(JSON schema style\):

```json
{
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
        "standard": {
            "type": "object"
        },
        "custom": {
            "type": "object"
        }
    },
    "required": []
}
```

‌

Example:

```json
{
  "parameters": {
    "standard": {
      "relaystate": "/myapp/home"
    },
    "custom": {
      "mycustomparam1": "customvalue"
    }
  }
}
```

‌

Full SAML object example:

‌

```json
{
  "urn:ietf:params:fastfed:1.0:provisioning:saml:2.0:enterprise": {
    "saml_subject": {
      "urn:ietf:params:fastfed:1.0:schemas:scim:2.0": "userName"
    },
    "desired_attributes": {
      "urn:ietf:params:fastfed:1.0:schemas:scim:2.0": {
        "required_user_attributes": [
          "displayName"
        ],
        "optional_user_attributes": [
          "phoneNumbers[primary eq true].value"
        ]
      }
    },
    "parameters": {
      "standard": {
        "relaystate": "/myapp/home"
      },
      "custom": {
        "mycustomparam1": "customvalue"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

‌

